  "notes": "Sequence transcribed from the official Occupational Therapy Assistant Program Handbook 2026-2027 (published at anokatech.edu, retrieved 2026-10-01), 'Sequencing Plan for Cohort Beginning in Fall of 2026'. Faculty recommend students take as many general education courses as possible before the OTA course sequence, but this is not required. All OTA courses require a minimum grade of C (80%) to pass and progress; all general education courses must be completed before the third didactic semester (Fall of year 2); HLTH 1005 must be passed with a 2.0 (80%) or higher before moving to second-semester OTA coursework. Each semester's courses are prerequisites to the following semester's courses. Level II fieldwork rotations (COTA 2411, COTA 2421) are full-time, 40 hours per week for 8 weeks each; fieldwork requirements include vaccinations, CPR certification, and a Minnesota background check. Graduates are eligible to take the NBCOT certification examination to become a Certified Occupational Therapy Assistant (COTA). Spring Semester Year 1 is listed as '14-18 credits' in the handbook; the courses shown sum to 18.",
